      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Stabilized ref2va preset: upload character.png, background.png, speech.wav and appearance_reference.png. Use a clean image of the intended complete scene as appearance_reference, with comparable framing and lighting. It sets color and fine-detail statistics; it is not an extra Picture reference or a fixed opening frame. color_stabilization=0.35 and detail_stabilization=0.35 are starting values. Every chunk retains all image references. Generated visible frames receive bounded color/contrast correction and attenuation of excess fine texture, with correction smoothed across chunk boundaries. The corrected tail is re-encoded as motion context for the next chunk to counter accumulating drift. Reduce detail_stabilization if too soft; reduce color_stabilization if the grade is too strong. These filters cannot reconstruct lost detail or guarantee identity. Source audio remains locked and unchanged; the Exact Audio MKV saver preserves decoded input samples, channels and sample rate. Use a desktop player supporting MKV/PCM. See docs/ref2va-lipsync.md."
      ],
      "title": "Ref2VA lip sync with exact source audio"
    },
